cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use or reference DRA (Document Reliability Assurance) or DRA-GC-1
  in your work, please cite this repository as below. This is a
  research-stage artefact; see docs/dra/DRA-PUBLIC-CLAIMS.md for the
  publication-safe description of what has and has not been demonstrated.
  This citation covers both the software (MIT-licensed) and the manuscript/
  documentation (CC-BY-4.0-licensed); see docs/dra/DRA-LICENSING.md for the
  complete licensing boundary, including the third-party material this
  licence does not cover.
type: software
title: >-
  DRA (Document Reliability Assurance): A Deterministic, Evidence-Auditable
  Approach to Assessing Claim Support in Machine- and Human-Consumed
  Documents
authors:
  - family-names: Rasmussen
    given-names: Cristina
abstract: >-
  DRA is a research-stage reference evaluator that assesses documents
  against a defined set of reliability issue classes (evidence absence,
  evidence inadequacy, and internal claim inconsistency, out of nine
  formally defined) using a deterministic, eight-stage evaluation pipeline
  bound to cryptographically verifiable proof receipts. This citation
  covers DRA-GC-1, the first frozen, publication-candidate evaluator state
  (version 0.1.2), and its accumulated internal evidence base: a
  33-document development corpus, a documented robustness programme, and
  two internal, pre-registered, contamination-blind generalisation studies
  (DRA-GEN-001, DRA-VAL-002) totalling 100 blindly-evaluated documents.
  No external, third-party validation has yet been performed; see the
  manuscript's Limitations section for the complete disclosed scope.
version: DRA-GC-1 (evaluator 0.1.2, pipeline 1.0, model/schema 0.1.0, corpus DRA-CORPUS-1.0.0)
date-released: "2026-08-12"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - document-reliability
  - evidence-auditing
  - authority-resolution
  - claim-verification
  - reproducibility
  - proof-receipts
  - deterministic-evaluation
  - machine-consumed-documents
identifiers:
  - type: other
    value: DRA-GC-1
    description: >-
      Frozen candidate identifier. Canonical aggregate digest:
      77544648dcb37caf96468123de4d19123becceff48f2023f6c885899350b857b
      (see docs/dra/DRA-GC-1-FREEZE-RECEIPT.md for full verification
      instructions).
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21918468
    description: >-
      Version-specific archival DOI for the DRA-GC-1 GitHub release,
      registered via Zenodo under DRA-PUB-010 (see
      docs/dra/DRA-PUB-010-ARCHIVAL-DEPOSIT.md). Concept DOI (all versions):
      10.5281/zenodo.21918467.
references:
  - type: report
    title: DRA-001 — Version 1 Programme Specification
    notes: docs/dra/DRA-001-VERSION-1-PROGRAMME-SPECIFICATION.md
  - type: report
    title: DRA-GC-1 Freeze Specification and Receipt
    notes: docs/dra/DRA-GC-1-FREEZE-SPECIFICATION.md, docs/dra/DRA-GC-1-FREEZE-RECEIPT.md
  - type: report
    title: DRA-GEN-001 — Blind Generalisation Study
    notes: docs/dra/DRA-GEN-001-BLIND-GENERALISATION-PROTOCOL.md, docs/dra/DRA-GEN-001-POST-BLIND-EVIDENCE-REVIEW.md
  - type: report
    title: DRA-VAL-002 — English-HTML Blind Validation Study
    notes: docs/dra/DRA-VAL-002-ENGLISH-HTML-VALIDATION-PROTOCOL.md, docs/dra/DRA-VAL-002-ENGLISH-HTML-BLIND-VALIDATION-REPORT.md
  - type: report
    title: DRA-PUB-003 Manuscript
    notes: >-
      docs/dra/DRA-PUB-003-MANUSCRIPT.md — canonical frozen scientific source,
      identifier DRA-PUB-MANUSCRIPT-1, SHA-256
      5aa6cf64b3e985dca5178db6aeb1487a8103782105d968ed62625457eb8e4f8e (see
